// City Computer — Prisma schema entry point.
// Multi-file schema (docs/04-REPOSITORY-STRUCTURE.md §4). Prisma 7 reads every
// `.prisma` file in this directory as one logical schema — models, enums, and
// relations are shared across files without any import statement.
//
// This file owns the datasource, the generator, and every enum. Enums are
// grouped by domain purely for human navigation; Prisma has a single global
// enum namespace regardless of which file declares them.
//
// Conventions applied throughout every file in this directory
// (docs/06-DATA-MODEL.md §1):
//   - Primary keys:      id String @id @default(cuid(2))
//   - Money:              Int, paisa, field name ends "Paisa"
//   - Timestamps:          createdAt/updatedAt on everything that has them
//   - Soft delete:         deletedAt ONLY on Product, Variant, Category,
//                          Brand, Post, Page, Customer, ComponentPart
//   - Optimistic lock:     version Int @default(0) on Product, Variant,
//                          StockLevel, Order
//   - Naming:              PascalCase singular model, snake_case plural
//                          table via @@map, snake_case column via @map
//   - Enums:               PascalCase type, SCREAMING_SNAKE values
//
// Constraints Prisma's schema DSL cannot express (partial/filtered unique
// indexes, CHECK constraints, generated tsvector columns + triggers) are
// called out inline with `// TODO(raw-sql):` comments and collected into
// `prisma/sql/manual-constraints.sql`.

// Prisma 7: the old "prisma-client-js" provider (generating into
// node_modules/@prisma/client) is gone. "prisma-client" is the new
// Rust-free generator and `output` is required — see prisma.config.ts and
// docs/03-TECHNOLOGY-STACK.md for the rest of the v7 migration notes.
// Generated into src/generated/prisma so it's reachable via the existing
// `@/*` path alias: `import { PrismaClient } from "@/generated/prisma/client"`.
generator client {
  provider = "prisma-client"
  output   = "../../src/generated/prisma"
}

// Prisma 7: `datasource.url` (and `directUrl`) are no longer read from the
// schema file at all — the CLI (migrate/generate/studio) now gets its
// connection string from `prisma.config.ts` at the project root, and
// PrismaClient at runtime gets it via a driver adapter (see
// src/server/db.ts, which uses @prisma/adapter-pg with DATABASE_URL from
// the validated `env` in src/env.ts). Nothing needed here beyond the
// provider name.
datasource db {
  provider = "postgresql"
}

